course: dictionary
lesson: 8761
title: Seventy: seven tens
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Seventy is a number. It is written 70, and it means seven tens. Count in tens to 70: ten, twenty, thirty, forty, fifty, sixty, seventy. «Each kind of living thing has its own usual length of life: many people seventy, eighty or more.» Here seventy is an age.
explain: The seventies are the numbers from 70 to 79. A person who is 73 is in their seventies. Look at the first digit: in 7 tens there is a 7 in the tens place, so the number starts with 7 and sits between 70 and 79.
explain: Seventy can also be a speed or an amount of money. «An ostrich in danger runs at up to about seventy kilometres an hour.» Here seventy tells you how fast the ostrich can run. «Why has a game taken seventy pounds from my bank?» Here seventy tells you how much money was taken.
fact: Seventy means 70, which is seven tens.
fact: The seventies are the numbers from 70 to 79.
fact: «Queen Elizabeth II» reigned for «seventy years», so seventy can also be a length of time.
fact: When you read a number in a sentence, ask what it counts: money, years, kilometres or people.
fact: Seventy is written with the digits 7 and 0, and the 7 is in the tens place.
exercise: How many is seventy? | 700 | *70 | 7 | 17
exercise: «An ostrich in danger runs at up to about seventy kilometres an hour.» What is seventy measuring here? | *A speed | A height in metres | A name for a bird | A price in pounds
exercise: Which numbers are in the seventies? | *70 to 79 | 80 to 89 | 60 to 69 | 7 to 17
test: «Why has a game taken seventy pounds from my bank?» In this sentence, seventy is an amount of what? | Speed | Age | *Money | Time
test: A boy is 74 years old. Which group of ages is he in? | The eighties | *The seventies | The sixties | The twenties
exam: Seventy is seven what? | Thousands | Hundreds | *Tens | Ones
